        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 1053,
      "author": {
        "id": 1106949
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-02-16T23:37:26Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I hope this was named ec_image.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1053,
        "startChar": 5,
        "endLine": 1053,
        "endChar": 21
      },
      "revId": "42a29975e8dfc3fb8b35e8c8257c5540503cae65",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "9f6564ab_4665e2be",
        "filename": "include/ec_commands.h",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 1053,
      "author": {
        "id": 1314845
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-02-19T21:38:40Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "How about doing this?\n\n  #ifndef CHROMIUM_EC\n    #define ec_current_image ec_image\n  #endif\n\nThen we use \"ec_image\" internally and \"ec_current_image\" will still work externally.\n\nI don\u0027t really like using a macro like this, but maybe it\u0027s a stepping stone to fixing the external projects?",
      "parentUuid": "48f2e5cb_27d402c1",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1053,
        "startChar": 5,
        "endLine": 1053,
        "endChar": 21
      },
      "revId": "42a29975e8dfc3fb8b35e8c8257c5540503cae65",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "6b9a6302_baaf7662",
        "filename": "include/ec_commands.h",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 1053,
      "author": {
        "id": 1106949
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-02-20T17:45:50Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Or we define enum ec_image identically:\n\nenum ec_image {\n\tEC_IMAGE_UNKNOWN \u003d 0,\n\tEC_IMAGE_RO,\n\tEC_IMAGE_RO,\n\tEC_IMAGE_RW\n\tEC_IMAGE_RW,\n\tEC_IMAGE_RW_A \u003d EC_IMAGE_RW,\n\tEC_IMAGE_RO_B,\n\tEC_IMAGE_RW_B\n}\n\n/* Deprecated. Use enum ec_image. */\nenum ec_current_image {\n\t...\n}\n\nAnd after the transition, we remove the latter from ec_commands.h. I searched through the codebase and found \u0027enum ec_image\u0027 is available.",
      "parentUuid": "9f6564ab_4665e2be",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1053,
        "startChar": 5,
        "endLine": 1053,
        "endChar": 21
      },
      "revId": "42a29975e8dfc3fb8b35e8c8257c5540503cae65",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "028560d1_8f3da159",
        "filename": "include/ec_commands.h",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 1053,
      "author": {
        "id": 1314845
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-02-21T00:07:46Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Sounds good. We may also be able to set the \"deprecated\" attribute on \"ec_current_image\" as well to give a compiler warning.",
      "parentUuid": "6b9a6302_baaf7662",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1053,
        "startChar": 5,
        "endLine": 1053,
        "endChar": 21
      },
      "revId": "42a29975e8dfc3fb8b35e8c8257c5540503cae65",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "99bf9e0b_d71e07d2",
        "filename": "include/ec_commands.h",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 1053,
      "author": {
        "id": 1314845
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-02-21T00:16:14Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Actually, you can\u0027t make the definitions have the same name (EC_IMAGE_RO, etc) because enums in C are global:\n\n include/ec_commands.h:1067:2: error: redeclaration of enumerator \u0027EC_IMAGE_RO_B\u0027\n  EC_IMAGE_RO_B,\n  ^~~~~~~~~~~~~\n\n include/ec_commands.h:1058:2: note: previous definition of \u0027EC_IMAGE_RO_B\u0027 was here\n  EC_IMAGE_RO_B,",
      "parentUuid": "028560d1_8f3da159",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1053,
        "startChar": 5,
        "endLine": 1053,
        "endChar": 21
      },
      "revId": "42a29975e8dfc3fb8b35e8c8257c5540503cae65",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "1b3f84cf_5e09fb3d",
        "filename": "include/ec_commands.h",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 1053,
      "author": {
        "id": 1106949
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-02-21T03:24:20Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Hmm... That\u0027s right. I suppose your macro trick is a good step forward, then.\n\nLooking at the codebase, it wouldn\u0027t be much hustle even if we deprecate ec_current_image here today. I see only a few lines referring ec_current_image in each foreign project and none in mosys and depthcharge.",
      "parentUuid": "99bf9e0b_d71e07d2",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1053,
        "startChar": 5,
        "endLine": 1053,
        "endChar": 21
